wideband: companion above 16k with the holding off too

The auto-wideband gate only saw the held rate. With EVV_UPSAMPLE=none
a rate past outright synthesis (48k past 44.1k) comes back as nought,
so the gate counts nought the same as eleven thousand: sixteen thousand
itself stays native outright, everything above takes the companion,
whatever the holding says. Forty-eight thousand rides the companion
up from twenty-two thousand and fifty.
diff --git a/src/eci/synth/eci_synthwork.c b/src/eci/synth/eci_synthwork.c
index 80aa213..415b915 100644
--- a/src/eci/synth/eci_synthwork.c
+++ b/src/eci/synth/eci_synthwork.c
@@ -640,8 +640,14 @@ THIS int32_t stw_createAudioConverter(SynthThread *t, SampleFormat *fmt)
     /* The wideband voice engages by itself for anything above sixteen
        thousand: that is exactly where the checkbox used to engage it, since
        sixteen thousand itself is native outright and never took the
-       companion. No setting; the rate the caller asked for decides. */
-    wide = native == RATE_11025 && wanted > RATE_16000;
+       companion. No setting; the rate the caller asked for decides. With
+       the holding off a rate past what the engine synthesises outright
+       comes back as nought instead of eleven thousand and twenty five --
+       forty-eight thousand is past forty-four one -- and the companion
+       makes that too, so nought counts the same way. */
+    wide = wanted > RATE_16000 && (native == RATE_11025 || native == 0);
+    if (native == 0 && !wide)
+        return ERR_BAD_RATE;
     if (wide)
         native = WIDE_RATE;
 
